            "uid": "8a255500d712d0aeccb5fa8e",
            "title": "ollama/ollama: v0.40.12",
            "url": "https://github.com/ollama/ollama/releases/tag/v0.40.12",
            "published": "2026-10-27T00:07:12+00:00",
            "summary": "## Liquid AI LFM3 [LFM3](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3) is Liquid AI's new family of small models built for local agents, tool calling, and structured output, on Liquid's new tri-hybrid architecture. The family includes: - [lfm3](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3): a 1.7B text model with a 256K-token context window - [lfm3-vl](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-vl): adds image understanding - [lfm3-audio](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-audio): speech recognition, translation, and text-to-speech in 18 languages - [lfm3-omni](https://ollama.com/library/lfm3-omni): text, images, and audio in one model ```sh ollama run lfm3 ``` ## d1 decision models Liquid AI's d1 models now come in a 2B size, built on LFM3. [d1](https://ollama.com/library/d1) makes decisions about text and images, and [d1-omni](https://ollama.com/library/d1-omni) adds audio. ```sh ollama run d1:2b \"I was charged twice for order 4417.\" --ask \"Is this a billing issue?\" ``` Note: lfm3 and d1 2b are supported on Apple hardware in this release. Support for Linux/Windows coming soon. ## What's Changed - Faster prompt processing on Apple silicon for Gemma 4, Flint and Laguna models - Speculative decoding now supports DFlash2 draft models on MLX - Gemma 4 keeps more detail in small images - `ollama launch` now works with OpenCode v2 - Fixed tool-only assistant turns from Kimi CLI - Updated MLX and llama.cpp **Full Changelog",
            "source": "Ollama Releases",
            "kind": "research",
            "doi": "",
            "date_precision": "day"
          }
        ],
